          "choice": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A solar eclipse occurs when the moon passes between the Earth and the sun, blocking all or part of the sun's light. This alignment causes the moon to cast a shadow on Earth, creating phenomena such as a partial, total, or annular eclipse, depending on the observer's location and the distances between the Earth, moon, and sun. During a total solar eclipse, the sun's corona becomes visible, offering a unique astronomical event."
            }
